# Backend Conventions

- FastAPI, async, type-hinted. Pydantic models for all request and response shapes.
- JWT: short-lived access tokens, rotating refresh, asymmetric signing, validate
  issuer and audience. No secrets in tokens.
- Every endpoint enforces authentication and object-level authorisation. Default
  deny.
- Retrieval-first: query the corpus and vector store with module and as-at-date
  filters before any generation. Never answer a legal question from model memory.
- Every answer response includes its citation list and verified / unverified
  status.
- Deterministic legal values (deadlines, caps, thresholds) come from the rules
  layer, never generated.
- Disable or auth-protect `/docs` and `/openapi.json` outside dev.
- Rate-limit anonymous tool endpoints (abuse and cost control).
- Public `/api/tools/*` preview endpoints stay separate from the agent tool
  registry, but both delegate to the same deterministic core functions.
